## Sources and limits

University of Washington Radiology's individual [Muscle Atlas pages](https://rad.uw.edu/muscle-atlas) support the ordinary attachment and action facts. [UAMS's lower limb table](https://medicine.uams.edu/neuroscience/education/medical-school-courses/human-structure-module/anatomy-tables/muscle-tables/muscles-of-the-lower-limb/) corroborates the trochanteric fossa attachment of obturator externus. Main checked the indexed official UAMS page after a direct-fetch timeout; this is not an imported reference asset. These links establish teaching facts, not the identity or accuracy of a specific mesh. The UW obturator externus innervation field describes another muscle, so this batch makes no innervation claims. No nerve-root, pathology, diagnosis, procedure, imaging-visibility, registration, or observed-motion claim is included.

The BodyParts3D CC-BY-4.0 credit and source hold remain as already configured. All new question and explanation text is original project text under MIT; no UW or UAMS image, table, or other media was copied or imported. The UW images are copyright protected and have not been licensed for this batch. Source meshes represent named anatomy, not a demonstrated individual's attachments or function. Questions remain draft pending revision-bound radiologist review; no clinical sign-off or release approval is implied.
